---
permalink: /ui_kits/website/children-families.html
headline: Children and Youth
deck: From our youngest members to our teenagers, Emmanuel is a place where
  children and families are warmly welcomed into the life of the church.
intro_paragraphs:
  - text: Children and youth make up a core part of our church community at Emmanuel
      — and we know how much they have to teach us about spirituality and
      questions of faith.
  - text: '"For this reason we invest heavily in their Christian growth: for our
      youngest members through the Joyful Noise congregation, and for older
      children and young people through Children''s & Youth Church, singing in
      the choir, joining the serving team, and helping to lead the readings and
      intercessions at our monthly intergenerational worship."'
sunday_1030:
  eyebrow: Sundays at 10:30
  heading: Children's & Youth Church
  cards:
    - eyebrow: Ages 4–11 · Godly Play
      title: Children's Church
      body: Throughout term time, Children's Church meets during the 10:30 Sunday
        service. Our curriculum follows the Godly Play method of Bible
        storytelling — an approach which seeks to inspire curiosity and wonder in
        our younger members. It fosters a sense of the overwhelming love God has
        for all God's people, helping each child discover their own place in the
        story of faith.
    - eyebrow: Ages 9–11 · Up to Year 7
      title: Youth Church
      body: Youth Church typically involves some games, music and a lively exploration
        of the Gospel of the Day, or a chosen topic for the term.  Older children
        are welcome to join, but we find that by Year 7 they tend to be ready to
        join us for the service in church — singing, serving, or leading prayers
        and readings.
  steps:
    - heading: Arrive & be welcomed
      body: Our children's groups meet in the church building. A welcomer will guide you if you or your child are unsure of where to go.
    - heading: Off to their groups
      body: Children are invited to go to their groups during the opening hymn, and re-join their families at the distribution of Holy Communion.
    - heading: Sign in for next time
      body: On your first visit you'll fill out a short form. If you make Emmanuel your church home, we'll add their details to ChurchSuite for future signing-in.
  room_heading: The Harold Darke Room
  room_body: Children of all ages are truly welcome at every service. For those who need a break, this room — next to the kitchen at the back of the church — has books and toys, and is specifically set aside for children under 4. Come and go as you need.
  room_image: /assets/cms/site-images/room-hire-1.jpg
  room_image_alt: A quiet room set aside for young children, with books and toys
sunday_915:
  eyebrow: Sundays at 9:15
  heading: Joyful Noise · Ages 0–4
  intro: Joyful Noise is our lively, informal 9:15 service for pre-school
    children and their families, with music, movement and storytelling
    woven into a short, playful celebration of the Mass. It runs during
    term time.
  photos:
    - image: /assets/cms/site-images/children-youth-1.jpg
      image_alt: Pre-school children taking part in the Joyful Noise service
    - image: /assets/cms/site-images/children-youth-2.jpg
      image_alt: Families gathered together during the Joyful Noise service
    - image: /assets/cms/site-images/children-youth-3.jpg
      image_alt: A child enjoying music and movement at Joyful Noise
  steps:
    - heading: Arrive & be welcomed
      body: Joyful Noise meets in the church building. A welcomer will guide you if you or your child are unsure of where to go.
    - heading: Join in together
      body: Parents and carers stay together with their children throughout — there's singing, movement and a short, simple talk.
    - heading: Sign in for next time
      body: On your first visit you'll fill out a short form. If you make Emmanuel your church home, we'll add their details to ChurchSuite for future signing-in.
  room_heading: The Harold Darke Room
  room_body: Children of all ages are truly welcome at every service. For those who need a break, this room — next to the kitchen at the back of the church — has books and toys, and is specifically set aside for children under 4. Come and go as you need.
  room_image: /assets/cms/site-images/room-hire-1.jpg
  room_image_alt: A quiet room set aside for young children, with books and toys
feature:
  eyebrow: Thursdays in term time
  heading: Stay and Play
  body_paragraphs:
    - Stay and Play happens every Thursday in term time, 9:30 to 11:00am. This
      is a relaxed, friendly drop-in session with loads of great toys and
      usually a bit of a sing-song at the end.
    - It's a great way to meet other local parents and carers, and to get
      answers to questions about life in West Hampstead with kids. Coffee, toast
      and healthy snacks are provided, and one of the clergy or our youth worker
      is always around to host.
    - All babies, toddlers and pre-school age children, together with their
      parents and carers, are warmly welcome — with plenty of tea and coffee for
      the adults.
  image: /assets/children-families.jpg
  image_alt: Children gathered at the altar steps with clergy during an all-age service
callout_heading: Come and join us.
callout_body: Whether on a Sunday morning or at Thursday's Stay and Play, we'd
  love to welcome you and your family to Emmanuel.
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<title>Children and Youth — Emmanuel Church, West Hampstead</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
<style>
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); font-family: var(--font-sans); color: var(--ink); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }

  .cf-intro { padding: 96px var(--gutter) 100px; }
  .cf-intro .inner { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .cf-intro .lead-para,
  .cf-intro .intro-body > p:first-child { font-family: var(--font-editorial); font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.34; color: var(--ink); font-style: italic; margin: 0 0 30px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .cf-intro p { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--fs-body); line-height: var(--lh-relaxed); color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 22px; }

  .cf-glance { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 0; margin-top: 48px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 40px; }
  .cf-glance .item { padding: 0 32px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .cf-glance .item:first-child { padding-left: 0; }
  .cf-glance .item:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .cf-glance .k { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .cf-glance .v { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }

  .cf-sunday { padding: 110px var(--gutter); background: var(--cream); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .cf-sunday + .cf-sunday { border-top: none; }
  .cf-sunday .inner { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .cf-grouphead { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 52px; }
  .cf-grouphead h2 { font-family: var(--font-editorial); font-style: normal; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 14px 0 0; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1; }
  .cf-twocol { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; }
  .cf-twocol.is-solo { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .cf-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 40px 38px; }
  .cf-card .ages { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--brown); }
  .cf-card h3 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 30px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 10px 0 16px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .cf-card p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 16px; }

  .cf-plainintro { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 800px; margin: 0; }
  .cf-photorow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin-top: 36px; }
  .cf-photorow .em-well { aspect-ratio: 4/3; }

  .cf-expect { padding: 64px 0 0; }
  .cf-expect .head { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .cf-expect .head h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--fs-h2); font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 14px 0 0; letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.02; }
  .cf-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 28px; margin-bottom: 44px; }
  .cf-step { border-top: 2px solid var(--brown); padding-top: 22px; }
  .cf-step .n { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 18px; font-style: italic; color: var(--brown); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .cf-step h4 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .cf-step p { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }

  .cf-room { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; background: var(--paper-warm); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .cf-room .txt { padding: 56px var(--gutter-wide,48px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; }
  .cf-room h3 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 30px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 14px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .cf-room p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; }
  .cf-room .media { min-height: 280px; }
  .cf-room .media img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }

  .cf-feature { padding: 110px var(--gutter); }
  .cf-feature.is-band { background: var(--paper-warm); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .cf-feature .inner { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .cf-feature .em-feature .media { aspect-ratio: 4/3; }

  .cf-admissions { padding: 100px var(--gutter); }
  .cf-admissions .inner { max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; }
  .cf-admissions h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 40px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin: 14px 0 0; letter-spacing: -0.015em; line-height: 1.05; }
  .cf-admissions p { font-size: var(--fs-body); line-height: var(--lh-relaxed); color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .cf-admissions p a { color: var(--brown); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .placeholder-link { color: var(--brown); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--brown-soft); font-style: italic; }

  .cf-dbs { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 28px; padding: 40px 44px; background: var(--cream); border: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 8px; }
  .cf-dbs .ic { width: 56px; height: 56px; flex-shrink: 0; color: var(--brown); margin-top: 2px; }
  .cf-dbs .ic svg { width: 100%; height: 100%; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.5; fill: none; }
  .cf-dbs p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; max-width: 56em; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .cf-intro .inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; }
    .cf-twocol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
    .cf-photorow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    .cf-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    .cf-admissions .inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; }
    .cf-glance { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    .cf-glance .item { padding: 0; border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 20px; }
    .cf-glance .item:last-child { border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0; }
    .cf-room { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .cf-room .media { min-height: 200px; order: -1; }
    .cf-dbs { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px; }
  }
</style>
<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/assets/favicon.ico" />
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/assets/favicon-32.png" />
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/assets/apple-touch-icon.png" />
</head>
<body>

{% include "header.njk" %}

  <!-- Page head -->
  <section class="em-pagehead em-pagehead--band">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="em-breadcrumb">
        <a href="index.html">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="#">Get Involved</a><span class="sep">/</span>
        <span>Children and Youth</span>
      </div>
      <h1 data-editable="text" data-prop="headline" data-type="span">{{ headline }}</h1>
      <p class="deck" data-editable="text" data-prop="deck" data-type="text">{{ deck }}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Intro -->
  <section class="cf-intro">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="intro-body">
        <div data-editable="array" data-prop="intro_paragraphs">
        {% for para in intro_paragraphs %}
          <p data-editable="array-item">
            <span data-editable="text" data-prop="text" data-type="text">{{ para.text if para.text else para }}</span>
          </p>
        {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cf-glance">
        <div class="item">
          <div class="k">Sundays, 10:30</div>
          <p class="v">Children's &amp; Youth Church (ages 4–11), term time</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <div class="k">Joyful Noise</div>
          <p class="v">Sundays 9:15, for pre-schoolers</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <div class="k">Stay &amp; Play</div>
          <p class="v">Thursdays 9:30–11:00am, term time</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="service-times.html" class="em-readmore" style="margin-top:24px">See all service times →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Sundays 10:30 -->
  <section class="cf-sunday">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="cf-grouphead">
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">{{ sunday_1030.eyebrow }}</div>
        <h2>{{ sunday_1030.heading }}</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cf-twocol">
        {% for card in sunday_1030.cards %}
        <div class="cf-card">
          {% if card.eyebrow %}<div class="ages">{{ card.eyebrow }}</div>{% endif %}
          {% if card.title %}<h3>{{ card.title }}</h3>{% endif %}
          {% for para in card.body.split("\n\n") %}<p>{{ para }}</p>{% endfor %}
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      <!-- What to expect -->
      <section class="cf-expect">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="em-ornament is-leading">What to expect</div>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-steps">
          {% for step in sunday_1030.steps %}
          <div class="cf-step">
            <div class="n">{{ ["i.", "ii.", "iii."][loop.index0] }}</div>
            <h4>{{ step.heading }}</h4>
            <p>{{ step.body }}</p>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="cf-room">
          <div class="txt">
            <h3>{{ sunday_1030.room_heading }}</h3>
            <p>{{ sunday_1030.room_body }}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="media"><img src="{{ sunday_1030.room_image }}" alt="{{ sunday_1030.room_image_alt }}" /></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Sundays 9:15 -->
  <section class="cf-sunday">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="cf-grouphead">
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">{{ sunday_915.eyebrow }}</div>
        <h2>{{ sunday_915.heading }}</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="cf-plainintro">{{ sunday_915.intro }}</p>

      {% if sunday_915.photos and sunday_915.photos.length %}
      <div class="cf-photorow">
        {% for photo in sunday_915.photos %}
        <div class="em-well"><img src="{{ photo.image }}" alt="{{ photo.image_alt }}" /></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}

      <!-- What to expect -->
      <section class="cf-expect">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="em-ornament is-leading">What to expect</div>
        </div>
        <div class="cf-steps">
          {% for step in sunday_915.steps %}
          <div class="cf-step">
            <div class="n">{{ ["i.", "ii.", "iii."][loop.index0] }}</div>
            <h4>{{ step.heading }}</h4>
            <p>{{ step.body }}</p>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div class="cf-room">
          <div class="txt">
            <h3>{{ sunday_915.room_heading }}</h3>
            <p>{{ sunday_915.room_body }}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="media"><img src="{{ sunday_915.room_image }}" alt="{{ sunday_915.room_image_alt }}" /></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Stay and Play -->
  <section class="cf-feature is-band">
    <div class="inner">
      <div class="em-feature">
        <div class="media em-well"><img src="{{ feature.image }}" alt="{{ feature.image_alt }}" /></div>
        <div>
          <div class="em-ornament is-leading" data-editable="text" data-prop="feature.eyebrow" data-type="span">{{ feature.eyebrow }}</div>
          <h2 data-editable="text" data-prop="feature.heading" data-type="span">{{ feature.heading }}</h2>
          {% for para in feature.body_paragraphs %}
          <p>{{ para.text if para.text else para }}</p>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Seasonal workshops -->
  <section class="cf-admissions" style="padding: 90px var(--gutter) 0;">
    <div class="inner">
      <div>
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">Throughout the year</div>
        <h2>Seasonal workshops</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>In addition to our regular Sunday offerings, we run a number of seasonal workshops through the year — from our St Nicholas' workshop in Advent right through to Good Friday.</p>
        <p>These arts and crafts workshops are open to children of all ages. They're great fun, and always include a suitable amount of messy craft!</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Cubs & Scouts -->
  <section class="cf-admissions" style="padding: 90px var(--gutter) 0;">
    <div class="inner">
      <div>
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">Tuesdays</div>
        <h2>Cubs &amp; Scouts</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The West Hampstead Cubs &amp; Scouts group. Cubs &amp; Scouts meet at 6:30pm on Tuesdays at St Cuthbert's.</p>
        <div class="media em-well" style="margin-top:18px"><img src="/assets/cms/site-images/cubs-scouts.jpg" alt="The West Hampstead Cubs and Scouts group" /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Safeguarding note -->
  <section style="padding: 80px var(--gutter) 0;">
    <div style="max-width:1320px;margin:0 auto">
      <div class="cf-dbs">
        <div class="ic"><svg viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 8-7 10-4-2-7-5.5-7-10V6l7-3z" /><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" /></svg></div>
        <p>All our children and youth church leaders are DBS-checked volunteers, some of whom have professional backgrounds in education or childcare. Safeguarding the care of children and vulnerable people is taken very seriously at Emmanuel.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- School admissions -->
  <section class="cf-admissions">
    <div class="inner">
      <div>
        <div class="em-ornament is-leading">For school applications</div>
        <h2>Church attendance &amp; CofE school admissions</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>If you are considering applying to a Church of England primary or secondary school, please make sure you read the admissions policy of the school, because their criteria vary. <a href="#" class="placeholder-link">Admissions Policy for Emmanuel CofE Primary School — link to follow</a>.</p>
        <p>If you would like to register your child's attendance for the purposes of school applications, please make sure your child is registered with us on ChurchSuite. You will then be able to sign them in at any of our Sunday services. If you have any questions about registering your child, please contact the parish office.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="em-callout">
    <div class="inner">
      <div>
        <h3 data-editable="text" data-prop="callout_heading" data-type="span">{{ callout_heading }}</h3>
        <p data-editable="text" data-prop="callout_body" data-type="text">{{ callout_body }}</p>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <a href="contact.html" class="em-btn em-btn--tan">Contact the parish office</a>
        <a href="service-times.html" class="em-btn em-btn--ghost-light">Service times</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

{% include "footer.njk" %}

</body>
</html>
